        " رِوَايَةِ مُحَمَّدِ بْنِ عَطِيَّةَ عَنْ زُرَارَةَ عَنْ أَبِي جَعْفَرٍ عَلَيْهِ اَلسَّلاَمُ قَالَ: \"إِنَّمَا حَرَّمَ اَللَّهُ عَزَّ وَ جَلَّ اَلرِّبَا لِئَلاَّ يَذْهَبَ اَلْمَعْرُوفُ\"."
      ],
      "translations": {
        "en.bab-ul-qaim-publications": [
          "Hadith.4936 - In the narration of Muhammad ibn Atiyyah from Zurara, from Abu Ja'far Imam Muhammad ibn Ali Al-Baqir (as), he said:\n\"Indeed, Allah (swt), the Mighty and Majestic, only forbade usury so that acts of kindness would not disappear.\""
